-- Seed the Chaos Lab with starter experiments. Runs once, on the first `migrate deploy`.
INSERT INTO "ChaosExperiment" ("id", "title", "category", "difficulty", "description", "hypothesis") VALUES
('seedchaos01', 'Kill the DB container while the app is writing', 'containers', 1,
 $$Start a loop that writes rows through your app (or `psql` in a loop), then `docker kill` the database container mid-write. Bring it back with `docker compose up -d db`.$$,
 $$The app returns errors while the DB is down and recovers on its own once it is back. No committed row is lost.$$),
('seedchaos02', 'Get a container OOM-killed', 'containers', 1,
 $$Run a container with `--memory=50m` and make it allocate more (e.g. `python3 -c "x = 'a' * 200_000_000"`). Find the evidence with `docker inspect` and `dmesg`.$$,
 $$The process is killed with exit code 137, and docker inspect shows OOMKilled: true.$$),
('seedchaos03', 'Delete a named volume and recreate the stack', 'containers', 1,
 $$`docker compose down`, `docker volume rm` the database volume, then `docker compose up -d`. Then restore your data.$$,
 $$The stack starts with an empty database. Data is only recoverable from a backup.$$),
('seedchaos04', 'Image builds, app crashes on start', 'containers', 2,
 $$Break the Dockerfile so the build still succeeds but the app can't start: wrong `CMD`, a missing file, the wrong working directory. Debug it only with `docker logs`, `docker inspect` and `docker run --entrypoint sh`.$$,
 $$The container restarts in a loop; the logs point to the missing piece.$$),
('seedchaos05', 'Run out of PIDs in a container', 'containers', 2,
 $$Start a container with `--pids-limit=50` and run a fork loop inside it. Watch what the host and other containers see.$$,
 $$New processes fail with "Resource temporarily unavailable"; the host is unaffected.$$),
('seedchaos06', 'Two containers on different networks', 'networking', 1,
 $$Put an app and its database on two different user-defined networks. Debug why they can't talk with `docker network inspect`, `getent hosts` and `nc -vz` before fixing it.$$,
 $$Name resolution fails because Docker DNS only resolves names on a shared network.$$),
('seedchaos07', 'Misconfigure a port mapping', 'networking', 1,
 $$Map the wrong container port (e.g. `8080:80` when the app listens on 3000) or bind the app to 127.0.0.1 inside the container. Find out which with `ss -tlnp` and `curl` from inside and outside.$$,
 $$Connections from the host are refused or reset even though the container is healthy inside.$$),
('seedchaos08', 'Break DNS inside a container', 'networking', 2,
 $$Point a container at a non-existent DNS server (`--dns 10.255.255.1`) or overwrite `/etc/resolv.conf`. Tell apart DNS failures from connectivity failures with `dig`, `nslookup` and plain IPs.$$,
 $$Requests by IP work, requests by name hang until a timeout.$$),
('seedchaos09', 'Fill a disk to 100%', 'storage', 2,
 $$Inside a VM or a container with a small volume, fill the disk with `fallocate -l` or `dd`. See how the app, the database and logging behave, then find what used the space with `df` and `du`.$$,
 $$Writes start failing with "No space left on device"; the database may refuse connections or go read-only.$$),
('seedchaos10', 'Corrupt a config file', 'storage', 1,
 $$Introduce a syntax error into a config file (nginx, YAML, JSON) and reload or restart the service. Then do it again and use the tool's own validation (`nginx -t`, a linter) before reloading.$$,
 $$A reload keeps the old config running; a restart fails with a parse error pointing to the line.$$),
('seedchaos11', 'Start the app with a missing env variable', 'config', 1,
 $$Remove one required variable (database URL, secret) from `.env` and start the stack. Check how quickly and clearly the app tells you what's wrong.$$,
 $$Either it fails fast with a clear message, or it starts and fails on the first request. Find out which.$$),
('seedchaos12', 'Rotate the DB password without telling the app', 'config', 2,
 $$Change the database user's password with `ALTER USER ... PASSWORD`, leave the app config alone and watch what happens to open connections and new ones. Then roll it out properly.$$,
 $$Existing connections keep working; new connections fail with an authentication error.$$),
('seedchaos13', 'Wrong image tag: ImagePullBackOff', 'kubernetes', 1,
 $$Deploy a pod or deployment with an image tag that doesn't exist. Diagnose with `kubectl describe pod` and `kubectl get events`.$$,
 $$The pod stays in ErrImagePull / ImagePullBackOff and the events say why.$$),
('seedchaos14', 'Liveness probe that always fails', 'kubernetes', 2,
 $$Point a liveness probe at a path that returns 500 (or a wrong port). Watch the restart count and find the cause from events and `kubectl logs --previous`.$$,
 $$The pod goes into CrashLoopBackOff with growing back-off between restarts.$$),
('seedchaos15', 'CPU limit far too low', 'kubernetes', 2,
 $$Set `resources.limits.cpu: 10m` on a deployment and send it some traffic. Measure latency and look for throttling (`kubectl top`, container_cpu_cfs_throttled metrics).$$,
 $$The pod stays Running but is throttled hard: slow responses, probes may time out.$$),
('seedchaos16', 'NetworkPolicy that blocks everything', 'kubernetes', 3,
 $$Apply a default-deny NetworkPolicy in a namespace (needs a CNI that enforces policies). Then open only the traffic that's really needed, including DNS.$$,
 $$All pod-to-pod traffic and DNS lookups fail until you add explicit allow rules.$$),
('seedchaos17', 'Push a commit that fails the pipeline', 'ci', 1,
 $$Deliberately break a test, a lint rule or the build, push it and fix it from the CI logs alone, without running it locally first.$$,
 $$The pipeline fails at the right step and the log is enough to find the problem.$$),
('seedchaos18', 'Let a CI secret expire', 'ci', 2,
 $$Revoke or rotate a token your pipeline uses (registry, deploy key, cloud credentials) and run the pipeline. Make the failure obvious, then set up a safer rotation.$$,
 $$The job fails at the step that uses the secret with an auth error that doesn't name the secret.$$),
('seedchaos19', 'Restore last night''s backup into a fresh database', 'backups', 2,
 $$Take the newest dump, restore it into a brand-new database or container and check the data: row counts, the latest records, that the app starts against it.$$,
 $$The restore works and the data matches up to the time of the backup. Note how long it took.$$),
('seedchaos20', 'Find out how much data a backup loses', 'backups', 2,
 $$Write some data, take a backup, write more, then destroy the database and restore. Work out what your real recovery point is and whether it's acceptable.$$,
 $$Everything after the last backup is gone; the gap equals the backup interval.$$),
('seedchaos21', 'Leak a secret into an image layer', 'security', 3,
 $$`COPY` a fake `.env` into an image, delete it in a later layer, then recover it with `docker history` and by unpacking the layers (`docker save`). Fix it with `.dockerignore` or build secrets.$$,
 $$The file is still readable in the earlier layer even though the final image doesn't show it.$$);
